{
 "_": [
  "IA-P4 review (R3, R9) — the cases the period evolution's main fixture does not hold, in a book of their own so",
  "fixture-ledger.json (and ttr-demo's copy) stay as they were. Worked in README.md § The cases fixture; the expected",
  "rows (expected-cases-average.csv, expected-cases-fifo.csv) are printed by reference.py, never by the code under test.",
  "Window 2025-07-01 … 2025-12-31 (six months, two quarters), opening 2025-06-30, everything in CZK (no rate needed).",
  "P3 — same-day movements whose ids sort against what happened (R3): a buy and its storno on one day (`SST` sorts",
  "before `SUB`) of an instrument not held (G) and of one held (X); a buy and a sale of a new instrument on one day",
  "(H, `RED` before `SUB`); a sale and a buy of a held instrument on one day (X 12-05 — average cost changes with the",
  "order, FIFO does not). P4 — an instrument the ledger does not explain (K: the provider holds 50, the ledger only",
  "sold 20) with no price on the window's opening: its cost is unknown, never 0 (R9).",
  "IA-P4b review (R1, R7, RR4): P5 — a cash-account contract, whose fees arrive on BOTH legs (DistrInfo's cash debit `<Id>`",
  "and its deposits-detail twin `DEB<Id>`, one payment): an entry fee twinned by id (07-01), a cash-only fee (08-05), a",
  "commission twinned by day/amount/class with a hashed flow id (09-10), a flow and a cash commission that are NOT twins",
  "(10-02, the amounts differ), a named entry-fee variant (11-03, `vstupní poplatek` is a prefix), a plain withdrawal",
  "twinned on both legs (11-20, class other), the GFO contribution and a rounding credit on the cash leg (12-01), an",
  "entry-fee refund twinned on both legs (12-10). Each twin is counted once, from the flow. P6 — the provider counts a",
  "movement when it SETTLES (R7): a buy (Y 12-05) and a sale (Z 12-03) dealt more than 20 days before the 12-31",
  "valuation but settling after it, and a hand-entered buy with no settlement day (Y 12-20) still settling unseen."
 ],
